                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game's a complete mess..\nIt seems that it's composed of tons of elements completely unlinked to each other, and none of them make any sense.\nApart from the fact that it contains lots of text in Cyrillic script so well, not that great for a non-Russian speaker, even every question and cutscene in English is completely nonsense.\nThe music is overall completely annoying, and you can't turn it off - the main screen features a settings option, which only allows you to choose from windowed and full screen mode and to learn that the only control you'll be able to use is the left mouse button. \nYou will also told that the Espace (sic) key is used to exit. And by the way the game won't remember your settings, so it will always start as a new game in full screen mode.\nBut it's not just a matter of errors and non-polished stuff, it's the whole game that makes no sense at all.\nOn starting a new game, you'll choose from easy to hard money and a particular business plan (there's four of them); you'll then be thrown into a list of data and, after that one, the \"game\" begins.\nThe game is like a visual novel with a red text and everything drawn in Paint, with artworks that I haven't seen since the poorest indie '90s games. It's literally unplayable.\nYou'll then be asked to answer to questions, about 15 questions per \"game\", related to what you chose in the first place and what you saw before the actual game began. And then, everything will end.\nThe questions, being the \"business plans\" so limited, are of course extremely limited too but they aren't funny or anything else, they aren't real questions but just a bunch of Engrish/Russian words and well, after having chosen the one you preferred (?) between usually 3 or 4 possible answers for 15 times or something, the game will end. \nSo, press Esc, repeat on another business plan and in less than an hour you'll have probably earned every achievement and seen every thing that this crap has to offer.\nThe purpose should be that you're offered a plan, you've got to memorize it and then to answer correctly to the questionnaire, basically. I really can't think of a single reason why this game should be paid for if one's talking only about the gaming experience, since there's no challenge and no fun at all.\nSo, it's a total mess, literally. There's nothing salvageable - the artwork is really extremely unworthy, the soundtrack is repetitive and annoying and the game/visual novel section is utter trash.\nAnd as I said, there's no replayability since even if you're so crazy to memorize the crap and answer all the questions, they keep on returning since there are only few \"game modes\" and they're extremely short..\nPlus, well, all that crap is often an entire screen of stupid and nonsense data, so you'd best look on a guide on Steam to answer correctly if you want to, since it's impossible to memorize all those lines. The whole game is grammatically speaking a complete disaster, and it's at times unreadable.. I can't speak for the Russian version of course, but since they sold it as full English supported.. \nA much greater reviewer than me entitled his review \"here's a quick review of this game, don't buy it\". Trust him, really. And watch his video, here on the review page, which is way better than my reviews of course! But the message in a nutshell is: don't buy this thing, since at best it will take you less than an hour to get all the achievements but, if you've got a life unlike me, that hour and that euro/dollar is definitely way best invested into other things like.. doing what everyone does instead of spending time in front of the worst games of the whole Steam xD\nAnd yeah, don't read the game store page. There's no memory to be trained, there are no meme references or pop culture hints, there's really nothing apart garbage here. Run away!! XD",
